※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4462

※ A tuple is a value and not a place: its members are registers, not room in
※ memory.  Assigning to one would mean binding the name to a tuple made of the
※ others and the new value, which is what writing that out does.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let p: mut 〈u8, u8〉 = 〈1u8, 2u8〉
    p⟦0⟧ ← 9u8
    p⟦0⟧
